            <ArticleTitle>Quantum Criticality in Resonant Andreev Conduction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>116802</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1103/PhysRevLett.119.116802</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Motivated by recent experiments with proximitized nanowires, we study a mesoscopic s-wave superconductor connected via point contacts to normal-state leads. We demonstrate that at energies below the charging energy the system is described by the two-channel Kondo model, which can be brought to the quantum critical regime by varying the gate potential and conductances of the contacts.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
